Response: chromebook-mullvad-wireguard Repository Architecture
This repository is a production-grade, self-healing WireGuard (Mullvad) VPN setup explicitly optimized for ChromeOS (Crostini) environments.
It handles network drops, DNS leaks, key rotation, and automated failovers without relying on the desktop Mullvad GUI.
Component Breakdown
1. Operations & Orchestration (Makefile, CHEATSHEET.txt, README.md)
Makefile: Central command runner simplifying setup, linting, testing, and cleanup.
CHEATSHEET.txt: Quick reference guide for common command-line operations and troubleshooting.
2. Systemd Service Integration (systemd/)
wg-mullvad.service: Systemd unit file to manage the primary WireGuard interface lifecycle (wg-quick up wg0 / down wg0) with security
hardening flags (ProtectSystem=full, CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_ADMIN CAP_NET_RAW).
wg-recovery.service: Watchdog daemon that monitors connection health and triggers dynamic server failovers if handshakes stall or
connections drop.
3. Configurations & Templates (config/)
wg0.conf.template: Default standard WireGuard configuration template using standard Mullvad endpoints (IPv4/IPv6).
wg0-advanced.conf.template: Multi-hop, custom DNS, and MTU-tuned configuration template for high-latency or restricted networks.
mullvad-servers.json: Cached local copy of Mullvad relay servers (updated via server-discovery.sh).
4. Automation Scripts (scripts/)
common-packages.sh: Centralized dependency manager that installs and verifies wireguard-tools, jq, curl, dnsutils, iproute2, and
netcat-openbsd.
server-discovery.sh: Queries Mullvad’s REST API for available relay servers, filtering by latency/location, with local 12-hour caching in
/var/cache/chromebook-mullvad/.
setup-resilient.sh: Primary deployment script that generates private/public key pairs, applies configuration templates, updates interface
settings, and enables systemd services.
validate-setup.sh: Pre-flight & post-flight verification script to check kernel compatibility (uname -r), required binary paths, and file
permission safety (600 on keys/configs).
test-resilient.sh: Connection test suite executing handshake checks, ping tests, DNS leak assertions, and HTTP egress verification.
performance-monitor.sh: Benchmarks packet loss, throughput, latency, and handshake age across configured servers.
update-keys.sh: Atomic key rotation utility that backs up existing keys, generates new ones via wg genkey, updates Mullvad API registration,
and restarts the service smoothly.
dns-leak-test.sh: Verifies that DNS requests pass exclusively through Mullvad's DNS servers (10.64.0.1 / 100.64.0.7) to prevent
Crostini system DNS leaks.
auto-recovery.sh: Background loop executed by wg-recovery.service to cycle through alternative servers when handshakes exceed
maximum age thresholds (default: 120s).
kill-switch.sh: Emergency script to immediately drop network interfaces and securely wipe local key material using shred.
wg-env.sh & lib.sh: Shared environment variables and logging/error-handling functions used across all shell scripts.
5. CI/CD & Testing (.github/workflows/ci.yml, .shellcheckrc)
ci.yml: GitHub Actions workflow that runs static analysis (shellcheck) and validates configuration syntax on every commit/PR.
Key Workflows & Commands
Deployment & Setup
# Bootstrap system dependencies, configs, and systemd services
make bootstrap
# Or run setup directly:
bash scripts/setup-resilient.sh
Monitoring & Health Checks
# Run connection and leak test suite
make test
# Monitor tunnel performance and latency
make perf
# View systemd service status
sudo systemctl status wg-mullvad.service
Security & Key Management
# Rotate WireGuard key pair safely
bash scripts/update-keys.sh
# Emergency network shutdown & key destruction
bash scripts/kill-switch.sh
